    "body": "Rule change, decided by the maintainer in the question dialog on 2026-11-12 (later the same day as PROCESS_VERSION 31): **\"Any collaborator review counts\"** and, on who may merge, **\"Both collaborators\"**. His words: \"everyone counts. everyone needs to get merged, mkinney and i are coolaboration across the world on the same code base\". So the owner-only rule of PROCESS_VERSION 31 is superseded: a review marker and a `merge-ready` label count when a COLLABORATOR (an account with write access; today NeoTech, mkinney, dudedagger42) posted them - on their own PRs too, as long as the review was done by an agent that did not write the change (AGENTS.md's existing rule) - and any collaborator's session may merge reviewed PRs with the `merge-ready` skill; release cuts stay with the maintainer. A marker or label from a non-collaborator still does not count. The process text follows in the PR for #1320 (PROCESS_VERSION 32); the rule applies from now.",
